// std.test — the M10a provision as a real source (B2a design D1-4,
// option A). assertEqual is declared here for the name's reach — mock
// targets and value positions resolve it — but its calls still ride
// importCall's dispatch ahead of the member gate: the call face's own
// typing (the first parameter fixes T, the Eq-domain gate, the same-type
// second parameter) is not a declaration's business. The empty bodies are
// the keyed fictions; codegen emits the call face directly.
pub fn assertTrue(cond: Bool) { }
pub fn assertFalse(cond: Bool) { }
pub fn assertEqual<T>(a: T, b: T) { }
